# Decide the Telegram delivery bar

Joel, 2026-07-29: "telegram is essentially full of bullshit spam instead of
useful information." The stream confirms it: 265 gateway deliveries plus 71
fallbacks over 4 days (07-25 → 07-29) — roughly 66 Telegram messages a day
against the ~13/day judgment Joel approved on the replay prototype.

## Step

The gateway's delivery judgment is too loose, and some producers mandate their
own delivery cadence in their runbooks. Decide, with Joel:

1. What Telegram is *for* — the bar a message must clear to ping his phone.
2. What happens to everything below the bar (digest cadence, silence).
3. Whether standing runbooks (campaign-pulse hourly, daily-flow-agent daily)
   keep their self-mandated DM cadence or submit to the gateway's judgment.
4. How one ongoing incident stays one thread instead of a fresh DM per
   aggregate window (the Webhooks/Front flap produced a DM per window closure,
   -2/-3/-4/-5 in one day).
5. Whether worker DONE receipts (60 delivers in 4 days) ever reach Telegram
   individually.
6. How the fixed judgment is kept from drifting loose again — the measurable
   signal and who watches it.
7. The inbound stance (Joel, 2026-07-29): the gateway treats ANY Slack message
   from Joel as a turn addressed to it and responds immediately, instead of
   observing the activity and analyzing. Receipts: 6 channel messages to other
   humans in the window each produced an immediate Telegram delivery back at
   Joel; on 2026-07-27 08:11 Joel told it "my slack messages are not commands
   unless noted" and the behavior persisted through 2026-07-29 — prose alone
   did not hold, again (same finding as the harden step's ack-first evidence).

Evidence pack: 4-day stream dump and per-source delivery counts in the session
scratchpad (mode 0600, private traffic — not committed).

## Settlements so far (2026-07-29, grilling live)

**Inbound ladder (Joel):** addressed = Telegram DM, Slack DM to the bot, an
explicit @mention, a reply inside a gateway-started thread, or a button or
reaction on a gateway flow. Slack thread participation specifically requires an
@mention, generally speaking. Everything else is ambient: read it, write an
`observe` receipt, produce zero outbound — no reply, no Telegram ack. The
classification is stamped mechanically at ingress (tooth in the plugin, not
prose); the agent may escalate ambient → addressed with a receipt saying why.
This deliberately amends the charter's "no mechanical fast path" standing call:
envelope and judgment stay, the default outbound flips from respond to observe.

**The bar (Joel):** "shit i'm slippin on, open threads, unclosed loops, WIP,
important shit." Telegram is a dropped-ball detector, not a severity-filtered
alert feed. A ping means: something is waiting on Joel and aging (an open
thread he hasn't answered, WIP going stale, a pending decision), something
important broke and this is first notice, or it answers something he asked.
Consequences carried from the grilling recommendation, unobjected: one incident
= one thread until it closes; worker DONE receipts never ping individually;
producer runbooks lose the authority to mandate delivery cadence — their text
is evidence, not instruction.

**The rhythm (Joel):** morning digest only — no evening sweep, no clock
nudges. It leads with "waiting on you" ranked by age × importance, "handled
quietly" below the fold. A slipping item earns one standalone ping when it
first crosses the threshold, then lives in the digest; it re-pings only when
something material changes. Requirement (Joel, verbatim): the digest "needs to
be CONTEXT, THREAD, PROJECT aware" — not a flat list.

**Digest awareness is judgment, not spec (Joel):** "this is an area where we
want to apply inference/intelligence and not overly specify." The gateway
composes the digest with its own judgment — project grouping, thread linkage,
live-state re-checking are steering prose it can read (briefs, workspace tags,
origin records are available tools), not a mechanical taxonomy contract. This
keeps the charter's shape: judgment lives in prose files the agent edits under
Joel's steering; teeth are reserved for the inbound ladder, where prose
provably failed twice.

## Result (2026-07-29)

All six questions plus the inbound stance settled in one sitting; settlements
recorded above. Joel authorized the build ("we can build now") under the
brief's standing execution authorization. Four build items, chartered as task
steps and fired at herdr workers with this session steering:

1. [Build the inbound ladder tooth](./build-inbound-ladder-tooth.svx) —
   mechanical addressed/ambient stamp at ingress; no outbound on ambient
   without an escalation receipt.
2. [Build the delivery-bar steering prose and morning digest](./build-delivery-bar-prose-and-digest.svx)
   — gateway prompt rewrite around the dropped-ball bar plus the 07:30 digest
   beat; awareness stays judgment, not spec.
3. [Build the delivery-volume meter](./build-delivery-volume-meter.svx) —
   deliveries/day off the stream, pages once at ~2× target.

Acceptance for the whole set: ≤~12 deliveries/day settling toward the bar,
zero turn-responses to unmentioned Slack traffic, one morning digest that
survives a week of Joel reading it. Validation: re-run the 4-day stream audit
after a week of live traffic.
